Spec: Core Layer

Purpose:
  Orchestration, Identity & Access Management (IAM), and HTTP Gateway for the MitM Data Aggregator. This layer operates as a single unified ECS Task.

Platform: Rust/Linux

Structure:
  ./mitm_http-server
  ./mitm_iam-server
  ./mitm_scheduler-server
  ./mitm_common

Must:
  `mitm-core-http` is the main container process (PID 1) and supervises `mitm-core-iam` and `mitm-core-scheduler` using `tokio::process::Command`.
  `mitm-core-http` immediately answers `HTTP 200 OK` on `/health` to satisfy AWS ECS checks.
  Initial configuration (`config.enc` or ENV) is parsed independently by each binary. `mitm-core-http` passes the configuration file path to the child processes via CLI arguments.
  `mitm-core-scheduler` owns and protects the Master Key (KEK) and provides DB credentials via the IPC Unix Socket (`/app/run/mitm_scheduler.sock`).
  `mitm-core-http` and `mitm-core-iam` run a retry/backoff loop to connect to the UDS sockets.
  `mitm-core-http` blocks all functional API routes (returns `HTTP 503`) until the UDS IPC connections are successfully established.
  Database logging in HTTP and IAM components starts strictly AFTER the UDS connection to the Scheduler is established. During initialization, all logs must be written to STDOUT.
  If a child process crashes, `mitm-core-http` logs a fatal error and exits (`std::process::exit(1)`) to trigger an ECS restart.
  On SIGTERM, `mitm-core-http` forwards the signal to its children and waits for their graceful shutdown.

Must not:
  `mitm-core-http` must not load or hold the KEK directly in its memory space.

Tasks:
  [ ] Rust (`mitm_http-server`): Implement ECS Supervisor logic to spawn IAM and Scheduler via `tokio::process::Command`.
  [ ] Rust (`mitm_http-server`): Implement `tokio::signal::unix` SIGTERM handling and propagate to child processes.
  [ ] Rust (`mitm_http-server`): Implement Retry/Backoff loop for UDS connections to `/app/run/mitm_scheduler.sock`.
  [ ] Rust (`mitm_http-server`): Implement 503 middleware for API routes while UDS is not ready (excluding the existing `/health`).
  [ ] Rust (`mitm_http-server`, `mitm_iam-server`): Ensure DB logging is delayed until UDS connection to Scheduler is active; use STDOUT until then.
